<title>UK: Sullom Voe oil liftings drop, no trips to NWE.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe oil liftings drop, no trips to NWE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brent Blend crude oil loadings from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal dropped sharply to 387,720 tonnes in the week ending July 22 from 469,222 tonnes the previous week.</p>
<p>Barrels were seen heading to U.K. ports and two tankers were destined to the United States, but no ship left for the continent.</p>
